== hash records a miss
hash: zzm: not found
rc=1
== a later hash obeys it, and says so
hash: zzm: not found (remembered miss: hash -r searches again)
rc=1
== running it searches past the miss; the hit replaces it
zzm-ran
rc=0
== a remembered hit
rc=0
zzm is D/A/zzm.cmd
== the process that recorded a miss searches again
hash: zzs: not found
rc=0
zzs-ran
== command -v and type record no miss
command -v: none
type: zzv: not found
rc=0
== running a missing command records no miss
zzx: command not found
rc=127
rc=0
== a remembered program that has gone is searched for
hash: zzm: not found
rc=1
== hash -d forgets one name
rc=0
rc=0
== hash -r forgets everything
hash: zzm: not found
hash: zzm: not found (remembered miss: hash -r searches again)
rc=1
rc=0
== a PATH with a relative entry is not kept
hash: zzr: not found
hash: zzr: not found
== shells writing at once leave a readable map
remembered: between 1 and 8
malformed lines: 0
== a map in use is touched when read; one unused for 30 days is pruned
in use: touched
hash: zzp: not found
unused: pruned
== BASH_PATH becomes the PATH, once
zzb-ran
PATH starts with it
BASH_PATH=unset
not in the environment
== a nested shell keeps its parent's PATH
zzn-ran
zzn-ran
